    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule: **reject creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with 409**. The repo already contained the acceptance test (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`) that fills a fresh city to 50 owners and expects the 51st to be rejected with 409.\n\nFollowing the existing `DuplicateHousehold` pattern for the OfficeFloor function-injection pipeline, I added four files and wired one step:\n\n1. **`EnsureCityCapacity.java`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose normalized city (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, matching `EnsureUniqueHousehold`) matches the built owner's city, excluding the not-yet-persisted owner; throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50.\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception.\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 builds a `ProblemDetail` via the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper and responds `409 CONFLICT` with `errors: [\"city\"]`.\n4. **`...CityAtCapacityException.yml`** (`officefloor/escalation/`) \u2014 maps the exception to its handler.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `ensureCityCapacity` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures or errors.",
